  <title>Products to reorder</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Reports</gui><gui>Products</gui><gui>Products to
  reorder</gui></guiseq> lists every product whose stock, over all locations,
  is at or below the <gui>Minimum</gui> set on the product (see <link
  xref="product_edit_main#inventory"/>). Products with no minimum set are left
  out. <gui>Reload</gui> reads the stock again.</p>

  <p>Select products and click <gui>Add to purchase order</gui>. Each one's
  <gui>Reorder qty</gui> is added to the open purchase order of its
  <gui>Vendor</gui>, the first vendor in its order numbers, or to a new one.
  If it is already on that order you are asked whether to raise the quantity.
  <gui>Ordered</gui> then reads Added. A product with no vendor or no reorder
  quantity is skipped, with a message saying which.</p>

  <p>Right click a product for its <gui>Product hub</gui>.</p>

</page>
